<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samuel Gorton</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1593">1593</a>–<a href="/years/1677">1677</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Samuel Gorton was an English religious dissenter and early settler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a>. Expelled from Plymouth, Portsmouth and Providence for his radical views and defiance of authority, he bought land from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narragansett-people">Narragansett</a> and founded Shawomet, later renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warwick-rhode-island">Warwick</a>, in 1642. He secured protection for his settlement from Parliament in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and led a small sect known as the Gortonites.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/samuel-gorton.jpg" alt="Samuel Gorton" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gorton.Samuel.Grave.Medalion.110721.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
